https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NWamoeeAIHs  (Capo 3)

There's also a version by Peter, Paul & Mary.  It's in G and has the (Bm).  It also has some minor lyric differences.  I think Gord's version is easier to play.

TIP:  In the intro strike you'll see a double chord with the first one in brackets.  This means strum the first chord once followed by a very brief pause and then strum the chord again for a full measure.

TIP:  The flourish at the end of each lyric can be skipped if you wish.

TIP:  The added (G) after the end of some words prior to the (A), e.g. "(G) heart (G)(A)" is there to remind you to strum an extra measure of (G).

    
